From a3de8b97324010ff44456da0907252f6f82e2785 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:59:41 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Add afdo_dump and afdo_merge v3 profile tools

Add the afdo_tools host component with GCOV AutoFDO v3 read/write
support and the first two command-line tools:

  afdo_dump   - print a GCOV AutoFDO v3 profile in stable order
  afdo_merge  - merge one or more GCOV AutoFDO v3 profiles into one

The shared profile model represents position counts, indirect-call
targets, inline callsite trees, source-name tables, and working-set
summaries.  afdo_merge remaps names and callee IDs into a common
namespace, recursively combines counts and inline trees, recomputes
summaries, and emits deterministic output independent of input order.
Readers validate file-backed record counts before allocation, and
writers report buffered output failures detected while closing files.

Wire --enable-afdo_tools so the top-level build can configure and build
afdo_dump and afdo_merge as a bootstrapped host module.  Profile
creation (afdo_create) and GCOV v4 support are added in later patches.

Regression tested on aarch64-linux-gnu with no new regressions.

ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.def: Add afdo_tools as a bootstrapped host module.
	* Makefile.in: Regenerate.
	* configure: Regenerate.
	* configure.ac: Add afdo_tools to host_tools.  Add
	--enable-afdo_tools.

