From 61c673944e6ec4c5a22ff962d4a2cbca6505dd3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:59:42 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Add afdo_create with BRBE/LBR profile ingestion

Add afdo_create, which turns offline perf branch-stack samples into a
GCOV AutoFDO v3 profile:

  - Add support for ARM BRBE and x86 LBR data from perf.data
  - correlate sampled addresses and branch ranges with ELF symbols and
    DWARF
  - attribute samples across inline callsite trees
  - emit GCOV v3 profile

Organize correlation by pipeline phase: keep the public correlator as a
small orchestrator, isolate diagnostics and GCOV export, co-locate sample
selection policy with bucketing, and keep profile-tree mutation behind a
narrow model API.

Compute working-set summary entries from nonzero leaf position counts so
GCC can derive meaningful hot-count thresholds from generated profiles.
Validate profile identity and retain deterministic symbol, callsite, and
GCOV materialization order.

Handle overlapping DWARF ranges with indexed lookups, split sampled ranges
at symbol boundaries, and route source locations through their inline
owners without retaining zero-count positions.  Correlate shared code ranges
once and export finalized profiles for every distinct ELF symbol alias.

Extend --enable-afdo_tools to build and install afdo_create, and require
libelf, libdw, and zlib when configuring afdo_tools.  Live LBR capture,
SPE ingestion, and GCOV v4 output are added in later patches.

Regression tested on aarch64-linux-gnu with no new regressions.

ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.def: Make GCC depend on afdo_tools.
	* Makefile.in: Regenerate.
	* configure: Likewise.
	* configure.ac: Mention afdo_create in the --enable-afdo_tools
