From 1dfab6312aad9025e36b2579b6a95d44f6a87998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:59:43 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Add live LBR profile capture support

Extend afdo_create so it can profile a workload directly, without a
pre-recorded perf.data file:

  afdo_create -b <binary> -o <out.gcov> -- <command> [args...]

Capture LBR/BRBE samples through perf_event_open and an mmap ring
buffer, then feed them into the existing branch-stack correlator and
GCOV v3 emitter.  Offline -p <perf.data> mode remains available; the
two modes are mutually exclusive.  Live capture requires kernel
branch-stack support and fails with a diagnostic when it is
unavailable; --sample-period sets the sampling period.

Regression tested on aarch64-linux-gnu with no new regressions.

afdo_tools/ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.in: Build live_branch_stack_reader into afdo_create.
	* src/afdo_create.cc: Accept a command after -- for live
	capture.
	* src/autofdo_options.h (profiler_run_options): Add
	live_sample_period.
	* src/autofdo_profiler.cc: Add a live-capture constructor that
	drives live_branch_stack_reader.
	* src/autofdo_profiler.h: Likewise.
	* src/live_branch_stack_reader.cc: New file.
	* src/live_branch_stack_reader.h: Likewise.

Signed-off-by: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Rahul Shinde <rashinde@nvidia.com>
