From 075c6a0f1d5730f885317dd5567fcb58a059db7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:59:44 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Add ARM SPE profile capture support

Add offline ARM Statistical Profiling Extension (SPE) support to
afdo_create.  Given a perf.data recorded with SPE AUXTRACE, decode the
packets, recover branch edges, synthesize ranges for the correlator, and
emit a GCOV AutoFDO v3 profile:

Regression tested on aarch64-linux-gnu with no new regressions.

afdo_tools/ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.in: Build arm_spe_aux_decode and perf_spe_reader into
	afdo_create.
	* src/afdo_create.cc: Add -s/--spe and --profiler to select the
	SPE reader.
	* src/arm_spe_aux_decode.cc: New file.
	* src/arm_spe_aux_decode.h: Likewise.
	* src/branch_stack_reader_base.cc
	(finalize_branch_edges_to_file_offsets): Split out of
	finalize_branch_stack_to_file_offsets.
	* src/branch_stack_reader_base.h
	(finalize_branch_edges_to_file_offsets): Declare.
	(finalize_branch_stack_maps): Also finalize when only branch
	edges were accumulated.
	* src/perf_file_reader.cc (create_perf_reader): Construct
	perf_spe_reader for sampling_mode::SPE.
	* src/perf_spe_reader.cc: New file.
	* src/perf_spe_reader.h: Likewise.

Signed-off-by: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Rahul Shinde <rashinde@nvidia.com>
