From 588628d832513caa955a77dbc9ff2b2c7918c84b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:59:47 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Add GCOV v4 read/write machinery

Add section-based GCOV AutoFDO v4 profile I/O to afdo_tools:

  - extend the shared profile model for v4 sections
  - add gcov_reader_v4 / gcov_writer_v4 for binary, compact, and text
  - teach the reader and writer factories to select v3 or v4

Existing afdo_dump, afdo_merge, and afdo_create consume v4 through the
factories without format-specific call sites.  Compiler-side consumption
of these profiles is added in the next patch.

The changes to the version 4 format with this patch are:

  (a) a self-describing, fixed-width section header table (the section type
      and compact flag are recorded in each table entry).
  (b) removal of the global compact flag from the file header (the byte
      becomes reserved) - the table is always fixed-width and per-section
      compactness lives in each section's bitmask.
  (c) two new section types, SECTION_INLINE_INDICES (a per-file-group reverse
      index of cross-module inline edges) and SECTION_INLINE_INDEX_TABLE (a
      directory locating each group's index section).

The summary and file-name sections also become ordinary entries in the
unified section table (no longer dedicated header fields).

The textual format gains one change: indirect-call targets now carry the
callee's name, so a symbol that appears only as an indirect target survives
a text round-trip.  It is otherwise unchanged.  The change in the format is:

  from  callsites = { OFF[.DISC] -> { ID = COUNT, ... }, ... }
  to    callsites = { OFF[.DISC] -> { "NAME":ID = COUNT, ... }, ... }

The formats of the new sections in the binary format are:

SECTION_INLINE_INDEX_TABLE (0x06)

One section per profile: a directory mapping a file group id to the section
index of that group's SECTION_INLINE_INDICES.  It lets a per-TU read find and
seek a single group's index section without reading every group's index.

  INLINE_TABLE_NUM_ENTRIES   int           number of mapped groups
  per entry:
    FILE_ID                  int           file group id
    SECTION_INDEX            int           index of that group's INLINE_INDICES

SECTION_INLINE_INDICES (0x07)

A per-file-group reverse index of cross-module inline edges.  One section is
emitted per file group (as defined by FILE_NAMES) that has cross-group
inliners: the set of top-level symbol ids (defined in *other* groups) whose
inline tree contains a symbol of this group.  Edges within a single group
are omitted (the group's own SYMBOL_INFO already carries them).

  INLINE_INDEX_NUM_INLINERS  int           count for this group
  INLINER_SYMBOL_ID          int  (x N)    top-level symbol id

In both section bodies "int" follows the section's compact flag (varint when
compact, big-endian otherwise), as for other section bodies.

Both sections are derived data: a writer regenerates them from the inline
tree, so a reader that does not need them simply skips the sections.  They
are emitted by default in v4.

Use: to read translation unit T, a reader takes T's own functions
(FILE_NAMES group for T) plus, via the table and index, the top-level
functions in other groups that inline any of T's symbols (which is the set
the auto-profile offline pass needs to recover cross-module-inlined
profiles) and parses only their SYMBOL_INFO.

Regression tested on aarch64-linux-gnu with no new regressions.

afdo_tools/ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.in: Build gcov_reader_v4 and gcov_writer_v4.
	* src/afdo_create.cc (write_gcov_output): Select the output writer
	through make_gcov_writer, so --gcov_version 4, --compact and
	--format text emit v4 profiles.
	* src/gcov.h: Extend the profile model for GCOV v4 sections.
	* src/gcov_io.cc: Add GCOV v4 I/O primitives.
	* src/gcov_io.h: Likewise.
	* src/gcov_reader.cc (make_gcov_reader): Detect and construct
	gcov_reader_v4 for binary and text v4 profiles.
	* src/gcov_reader.h: Declare gcov_reader_v4.
	* src/gcov_reader_v4.cc: New file.
	* src/gcov_writer.cc (make_gcov_writer): Construct
	gcov_writer_v4 for version 4 output.
	* src/gcov_writer.h: Declare gcov_writer_v4.
	* src/gcov_writer_v4.cc: New file.

Signed-off-by: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Rahul Shinde <rashinde@nvidia.com>
---
